  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nCold front continues to push SE across the area this afternoon.\nMost of the shower activity has weakened with the front \noriented parallel to the SW flow aloft. There could be a few \nT-storms popping up into early this evening along the far \nsouthern part of the area (southern Ulster, Dutchess, \nLitchfield) due to warm/humid and modestly unstable conditions \nthere as the front moves through. Cooler and less humid \nconditions will then filter into the region tonight, with a NW \nbreeze developing behind the front. Lows tonight will be much \ncooler ranging from the upper 30s in the W. Adirondacks to lower\n50s in the Hudson Valley. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure builds east across the area on Sat, providing dry\nconditions and seasonably cooler temperatures. Dry weather \nshould persist through much of Sun, with just a low chance for \nshowers well south/east of Albany Sun evening/night associated \nwith weak low pressure tracking east off the coast, and also \nnorth/west of Albany associated with an approaching cold front \nand upper level trough with limited moisture. It will turn \nbreezy on Mon, with below normal temperatures along with NW \nwinds gusting 20-30 mph. While it will be chilly Mon night, with\nhigh pressure positioned to our west a persistent breeze should\nprevent frost in valley areas. There looks to be a better \nchance of widespread frost in lower elevations Tue night, as the\nhigh moves overhead with light winds/clear skies expected. \nFrost Advisories and/or Freeze Warnings may eventually be needed\nin areas where the growing season is still active.",
